  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "The mean recovery time for injured runners is $\\overset{\u00af}{x}=70$ days with a standard deviation of $20$ days. What is the $z$-score that corresponds to a recovery time of $60$ days?",
  "worked_solution": "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{\u2015}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=60$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{\u00af}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{60-70}{20} \\\\  & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
